cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HyperGraSS / HGS2 / EIMDL or the accompanying 25-page research monograph in your work, please cite the software and monograph using this metadata."
title: "Evolutionary Information Minimum Description Length (EIMDL): Unified Seven-Law Lossless Genomic Compressor (HGS2 / HyperGraSS)"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: "Apache-2.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Islam"
    given-names: "Md Saiful"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MdSaifulIslamMSI/hypergrass-research"
url: "https://github.com/MdSaifulIslamMSI/hypergrass-research/blob/master/paper/HGS2_EIMDL_Research_Paper.pdf"
abstract: >-
  Open-source zero-dependency Java 21+ research engine (HGS2 / EIMDL, .hgs2 v2.0)
  uniting Generation 1 (HyperGraSS v1) and Generation 2 (RC-MDL v2) under Seven
  Formal Mathematical and Biological Laws (Laws I-VII) for lossless single-genome
  (Mode S), reference-conditioned (Mode R), and pangenome collection (Mode C)
  compression with exact 6-channel FASTA reconstruction. Includes the 25-page
  research monograph, 8 publication figures, 1,693-assertion automated audit,
  and reproducible Kaggle 15-codec cloud verification suite (winning 15/15
  bacterial tracks and compressing all 24 T2T-CHM13v2.0 | GRCh38 human
  chromosomes by 89.47x from 3.156 GB to 35.28 MB).
keywords:
  - genomics
  - pangenome
  - lossless-compression
  - minimum-description-length
  - arithmetic-coding
  - bioinformatics
  - java
  - chm13
  - data-compression
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Evolutionary Information Minimum Description Length (EIMDL): A Unified Seven-Law Theory and Bounded-Memory Architecture for Single-Genome, Reference-Conditioned, and Pangenome Compression"
  authors:
